<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The eleven reptile momo races (Big & Small pattern, 2026-09-20).

		Until now a reptile pawn was a vanilla Human pawn wearing a reptile xenotype:
		her body came from a gene body swap, and her corpse was an ordinary
		Corpse_Human shared with every human in the game. Each species now owns a race
		def, which is what lets her join the family's shared "momo corpses" line
		(ProjectMomo.MomoCorpses in the core mod), gives her own hide when she is
		butchered, and puts her body on the race instead of inside a gene.

		Each species is a ThingDef on ParentName="Human". It carries her body, her hide
		(leatherDef -> one of the four shared materials (dragon, lamia or lizardman
		scales, or the bunyip's own wool), the same one she sheds while she lives) and a
		BigAndSmall.RaceExtension naming her tracker.

		Which tracker, and why (user ruling 2026-09-20, "one row"):
		- The three plain species (lizardman, dragonewt, salamander) use a tracker of
		  our own, PMM_RaceTracker_<Species>, on ParentName="BS_DefaultRaceTracker" with
		  CompProperties_Race.canSwapAwayFrom. Their Health tab row names the species.
		- The five tailed and the three winged species use Big & Small's own tracker as
		  their ONLY tracker, set straight in raceHediff: BS_Naga_Race for a serpent
		  body, BS_HumanoidWithWings_Race for a winged one. That single def draws the
		  tail or the wings, brings the body's own stats (the serpent metabolism
		  package) and the VEF floating comp, and carries its own can-swap-away comp -
		  so the pawn shows ONE Health row instead of two. The accepted trade: that row
		  is B&S's label ("snake-person", "winged humanoid") rather than the species
		  name, which the Bio tab's xenotype still gives.
		- Giving them their own species-labelled row as well is what produced two rows;
		  merging the two into one custom tracker was tried on 2026-09-20 and CANNOT
		  work: a node is registered for XML inheritance only when it carries a <Name>
		  attribute (XmlInheritance.TryRegister reads "Name", never "defName"), and B&S
		  declares both trackers with <defName> alone. That attempt filled Player.log
		  with "Could not find parent node named BS_Naga_Race" and left the trackers
		  loading with no art, no stats and no comps.

		Bodies. The tailed species use BS_SnakeHuman, the winged ones
		BS_HumanoidWithWings_Body - exactly the bodies their genes used to swap to.
		That swap can no longer work: Big & Small only discards the Human def when it
		fuses bodies, so a gene thingDefSwap never fires on a pawn who has a race def
		of her own. The body sits here instead, so the tail or the wings are there
		from birth rather than a moment after generation. The tail and flight genes
		stay exactly as they are: their job is now the ability they grant and the
		ShowBase* flags that keep the B&S tracker drawing its art.

		Deliberately NOT here: size, temperature range, armour and melee tools. Those
		already come from the species genes (PMM_Gene_Reptile and friends), and a
		second copy on the race would stack with them.

		The race is assigned by xenotype: every XenotypeDef in
		XenotypeDefs/Xenotypes_Reptile.xml declares setRace (one of these defs) and
		forceRace true, and Big & Small applies it while the pawn's genes are
		generated. forceRace is required, not decoration: it is what makes the race
		beat the gene body swaps in the same swap pass.

		The pawn kinds still say <race>Human</race> on purpose, because one faction kind
		and one wild kind cover all eleven species. The xenotype is what picks the race.
	-->

	<!-- ===================== Tailed: serpent lower body ===================== -->

	<ThingDef ParentName="Human">
		<defName>PMM_Race_Basilisk</defName>
		<label>basilisk</label>
		<description>A venomous hunter of caves and deserts, with a serpent's tail in place of legs.</description>
		<statBases>
			<!-- 30 scales a corpse, the same count the insect momos give in chitin.
			     Her live shedding is separate (PMM_Gene_Reptile). -->
			<LeatherAmount>30</LeatherAmount>
		</statBases>
		<race>
			<leatherDef>PMM_Scale_Lizardman</leatherDef>
			<body>BS_SnakeHuman</body>
			<makesFootprints>false</makesFootprints>
		</race>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.RaceExtension">
				<!-- B&S's serpent tracker: the tail, the serpent metabolism, one row. -->
				<raceHediff>BS_Naga_Race</raceHediff>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</ThingDef>

